{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WEhsZWrPWfz9qpqW9B1Hww","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-579\"\n3\ttitle = \"The verdict carrier and the adjudication_review dial: gate over logged rounds, tree-bound trailer, generated rollup\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"strong\"\n7\tpriority = 9\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\tsupersedes = \"WI-558;WI-559;WI-560\"\n10\t+++\n11\t\n12\t## Deliverable\n13\t\n14\tThe merge gate reads the EVIDENCE and the evidence names the tree it judged.\n15\t\n16\t`kitlib/verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) is the verdict record's one home: the\n17\tnon-record tree identity — a SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r -z` with\n18\t`docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` dropped — the\n19\t`Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer\n20\tgrammar, the round-file / session-log join, and the branch-scoped readers. Two\n21\tcallers stand on it and that is the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` (may this\n22\tmerge?) and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` (does this lane still owe a\n23\tround?) asked one question with two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap\n24\tbetween them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n25\t\n26\t- **WI-558 DW1** — the gate computes over the branch's own round files,\n27\t  restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced: a file under\n28\t  `docs/reviews/` is a round only when the coordinator's own committed session\n29\t  log for that (train, ordinal) declares a REVIEW phase. Finding K closed —\n30\t  an implementer cannot author its own approval without also forging the loop's\n31\t  telemetry.\n32\t- **WI-558 DW2** — the machine half rides the round's own record commit as a\n33\t  trailer, written by the COORDINATOR and verified against its carrier's tree\n34\t  (the `Bar-Green` pattern). GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY: a verdict counts only\n35\t  while it names the branch's current non-record tree, read at the GOVERNING\n36\t  REV so neither the station refresh nor the commit that records the round\n37\t  stales an honest APPROVE. The freshness\n38\t  comparison is gone; there is no ordering rule left. The trailer is a\n39\t  CROSS-CHECK and never an accept path — one that contradicts the rounds\n40\t  refuses the merge.\n41\t- **WI-558 DW3** — `gen_verdict_rollup.py` (LLR-208) rebirths the rollup as a\n42\t  GENERATED artifact: `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, `trunk_step.py --regen`, a\n43\t  `check.py verdict-rollup` freshness step on the hook floor and in\n44\t  `_TRUNK_FRESHNESS_STEPS`, and `--check` with two answers. The gate never reads\n45\t  it, and the file says so where a human will see it.\n46\t- **WI-558 DW4** — the migration window: the gate accepts EITHER the round\n47\t  evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup, judged by the SAME identity rule,\n48\t  warning on stderr whenever the legacy path is what cleared it. Two\n49\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entries. The trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing.\n50\t- **WI-558 DW5 / WI-560 DW4 / WI-559 DW3** — `tests/test_verdict_record.py`\n51\t  drives each half beside its opposite (TC-205, TC-206).\n52\t- **WI-560 DW1** — ONE definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n53\t  verdict\", used by the merge slot AND the C2 review-owed derivation. That\n54\t  definition names a REV as well as a path set, so the station-refresh peel\n55\t  (`refresh_attestation` / `work_tip`) lives beside the fold and both readers\n56\t  call `governing_identity` rather than each choosing where to measure. The\n57\t  double-identical-round class is now unrepresentable, not policed: the commits\n58\t  that caused it cannot move the identity either reader compares.\n59\t- **WI-559 DW2** — a committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its round exactly\n60\t  as a committing BUILD does, under the dial; the phase stays in\n61\t  `NON_BUILD_PHASES` because a judgement is not a build. No exit banner claims a\n62\t  round that was never drawn — it counts them.\n63\t- **The dial** — `docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review`\n64\t  (`never` / `when-minting` / `always`; template and this repo ship\n65\t  `when-minting`), read through `agent_common.adjudication_review_owed` by BOTH\n66\t  the scheduler and the gate, with a closed vocabulary refused at preflight and\n67\t  a conservative fallback. Its `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row and the\n68\t  `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry ship with it. An adjudication lane drafting ordinary\n69\t  successors now merges with NO verdict artifact present anywhere — the OI-76\n70\t  acceptance becomes measurable on the next unattended run.\n71\t\n72\tReview A rework closed both evidence-boundary gaps. The loop's resume reader now\n73\tuses the same branch-scoped committed-path, logged-session and tree-bound entry\n74\tpipeline as the merge gate, so an approval-shaped file produced by a BUILD\n75\tsession cannot suppress the round the gate requires. The trailer's `rounds=N`\n76\tfield is now defined and checked as the completed review cycles represented at\n77\tthe governing tree (a dual-review cycle counts once, and rework starts the\n78\ttree-scoped count over); both the coordinator writer and gate derive that value\n79\tfrom the shared evidence. LLR-207's rationale now carries only the standing\n80\ttechnical reason, without the decision's provenance narrative.\n81\t\n82\tReview A round 007 closed four more, three of them one shape — a rule expressed\n83\tas a value something else got to choose. The identity's REV is now part of the\n84\tshared definition (the peel moved into `kitlib/verdict.py`, so a station refresh\n85\tno longer makes the two readers disagree); `branch_trailers` returns the ordered\n86\tSEQUENCE of attestations per tree, so the newest-first `git log` can no longer\n87\thand a reader a superseded stamp and have the cross-check accuse an approved\n88\tlane of forgery; and `tree_identity` passes `-z` while `fold_listing` takes\n89\tdecoded entries, so a quoted non-ASCII path can no longer fold a record file\n90\tinto the identity. The DONE banner states rounds DRAWN this run and the latest\n91\tverdict, because the tally it reads holds every completed round whatever its\n92\toutcome.\n93\t\n94\tVerifying finding 2's fix end-to-end found a fifth defect of the same family,\n95\tdriven and closed here. The refresh peel was TIP-ONLY, because `work_tip` is\n96\tshared with the `reset --hard` in `integrate.refresh` where peeling one commit\n97\ttoo far destroys work. So a telemetry commit — a `docs/iteration/` record path,\n98\twhich the fold exists to ignore — moved the governing identity anyway, by\n99\tBURYING the refresh under it: the loop answered `owed=True` and the merge slot\n100\trefused \"no logged review round names its current tree\", both readers agreeing\n101\ton the wrong answer and parking an honest APPROVE at a supervisor stop. That is\n102\tthe OI-76 failure mode itself, one commit further down than round 007 reached.\n103\t`governing_rev` now walks past that commit to reach the refresh, and `work_tip`\n104\tkeeps its tip-only contract untouched — the two shapes of the peel are separate\n105\tbecause a read-only reader can afford an answer a destructive one cannot.\n106\t\n107\tRound 012 found the same defect one commit SHAPE further on, and closing it\n108\tdeleted a rule rather than adding a case. The walk stepped by classifying the\n109\tPATHS a commit touched, so every commit whose paths it could not read — a merge,\n110\tan empty commit — stopped it. `commit_telemetry` writes exactly that shape: a\n111\t`Review-Verdict:` attestation must land even when the bookkeeping it rides is\n112\tunchanged, so it commits EMPTY, and the very commit RECORDING an approval buried\n113\tthe refresh underneath it. The step condition is now the module's own defining\n114\tsentence — a commit whose non-record identity EQUALS its first parent's cannot\n115\tinvalidate a verdict — measured directly from `tree_identity`. The empty\n116\tcarrier, the merge commit and the quoted-path trap stop being cases, because no\n117\tpath is classified in the walk at all. The regression drives the carrier through\n118\t`commit_telemetry` itself rather than a hand-made lookalike, and\n119\tPROCESS_OPTIONS.md's normative sentence is qualified to match the rule stated\n120\tbeside it: a commit that changes the non-record tree buys another round.\n121\t\n122\t`LLR-140`'s Approved detail cell was re-pointed IN-LANE: it asserted the retired\n123\ttime comparison, which nothing detects once it is false. Ratchet bumps\n124\t(`agent_common` 1272→1305, `agent_loop` 2519→2578, `integrate` 1298→1382 and\n125\tthen DOWN to 1352 when the peel left it, `check` 1163→1177, `bootstrap`\n126\t1658→1660, smoke membership 1480→1560) each carry\n127\ttheir reason at the entry; `_verdict_gate`'s complexity bump was REFUSED and the\n128\tfunction decomposed instead. Round-007 rework full suite, run at the tip\n129\t`cee19210`: 3343 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 615.27s — the failure is\n130\t`docs/stage` freshness, a trunk-lane artifact a work branch must\n131\tnot commit, bisected clean at the integration base. Account, deviations and the\n132\tone out-of-scope finding: `docs/log.d/WI-579-verdict-carrier-and-adjudication-review.md`.\n133\t\n134\t## Context\n135\t\n136\tMinted by the owner-directed backlog restructure of 2026-09-02 (plan of record `docs/plans/2026-09-02-backlog-restructure-and-consolidation.md` §2.2; executed out of band as a hand trunk commit series, not by a lane). The absorbed rows are archived under `docs/archive/work/restructured/` with their scope text untouched; their Done-when blocks are QUOTED below under their old ids and remain the spec this row must satisfy — decompose, don't paraphrase.\n137\t\n138\t**Why one row.** WI-558 Done-when 2 retires the gate's freshness comparison in\n139\tfavour of tree identity; WI-560 Done-when 1 builds one shared freshness\n140\tdefinition for the gate and the C2 review-owed derivation; WI-559 Done-when 2\n141\tmakes an ADJUDICATE commit schedule a round, which only means something once\n142\tthe round carrier WI-558 defines exists. Built apart in any order, the later\n143\tlane undoes part of the earlier one. Together: the gate and the review-owed\n144\tderivation read the SAME tree-identity trailer, and the round an adjudication\n145\towes is drawn under the policy below.\n146\t\n147\t**Adjudication review policy (plan §3, owner direction 2026-09-02).** The\n148\tadjudicator is already the cross-family judge by routing (`agent_loop`'s\n149\tADJUDICATE arm excludes the builder's family). A round over every adjudication\n150\tis a fresh session with less context judging the one session that held the\n151\twhole chain, and today it is also the supervisor stop on every unattended run\n152\t(`integrate._verdict_gate` demands a REVIEW-A from a lane whose phase is in\n153\t`NON_BUILD_PHASES`, so nothing produces one). This row adds\n154\t`docs/process.toml [attestation] adjudication_review = \"never\" | \"when-minting\" | \"always\"`\n155\t(template ships `\"when-minting\"`, this repo sets `\"when-minting\"`):\n156\t- `never` — no round after ADJUDICATE; the gate never asks an adjudication\n157\t  lane for a verdict.\n158\t- `when-minting` — a round is scheduled, and the gate demands its verdict,\n159\t  when the merged adjudication's `## Dispositions` drafts ANY successor whose\n160\t  `safety_class` is `spine` or `high-risk`, or when its `brief` is\n161\t  `consolidate`. An amendment verdict that only recommends a flip, a red-tc\n162\t  that drafts ordinary fix rows, a clean-close spot check: no round.\n163\t- `always` — the intended-but-broken behaviour today, made real.\n164\tOne reader function in `agent_common` (`adjudication_review_owed(docs, brief,\n165\tdrafts)`) serves BOTH the round scheduler (ADJUDICATE leaves the unconditional\n166\t`NON_BUILD_PHASES` set; the dial decides) and `_verdict_gate` (which consults\n167\tthe existing `integrate._adjudication_lane` plus the dial plus the merged\n168\tspec's drafts), so the two cannot disagree. Tests pin all three values on a\n169\tscaffold and pin that `never`/`when-minting` with ordinary drafts lets an\n170\tadjudication lane merge with NO REVIEW-A file present.\n171\t\n172\t## Done-when\n173\t\n174\t1. Every WI-558 Done-when item below, as written.\n175\t2. WI-560 Done-when 1 below, satisfied by the SAME trailer/tree-identity rule\n176\t   the gate uses (one definition, two readers).\n177\t3. WI-559 Done-when 2 below, under the `adjudication_review` dial.\n178\t4. The dial, its template row, `docs/enforcement-audit.md` row, and the\n179\t   `RESYNC_PACK.md` entry.\n180\t5. Full suite green; the OI-76 acceptance (three consecutive rows merged by\n181\t   one launch with zero supervisor commits) is measurable on the next\n182\t   unattended run.\n183\t\n184\t### From WI-558 (Done-when, verbatim)\n185\t\n186\t1. `integrate._verdict_gate` computes its predicate over the branch train's\n187\t   round files, restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced (the\n188\t   telemetry commit is the anchor) — an implementer-authored file in the\n189\t   review path is not a round (the plan's finding K closed).\n190\t2. The round's own commit carries the machine half as a trailer —\n191\t   `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=N tree=<sha>` — the\n192\t   existing `Bar-Green` pattern. GOVERNING = TREE IDENTITY as ruled: a\n193\t   verdict counts only if it names the branch's current non-record tree; no\n194\t   ordering rule; the gate's freshness comparison retires.\n195\t3. The per-WI rollup becomes a GENERATED artifact: a regenerator compiles it\n196\t   from the round files, `--check` keeps it fresh, it is declared in\n197\t   `docs/stack.ini [generated]`, and the gate never reads it. The supervisor\n198\t   prompt's hand-compile instruction retires in the same change.\n199\t4. Migration window per the plan's section 6: during the window the gate\n200\t   accepts EITHER the round-file evidence or a legacy hand-authored rollup,\n201\t   warning on the legacy path; `RESYNC_PACK.md` carries the entry. The\n202\t   trailer is additive and costs an adopter nothing until their loop writes\n203\t   one.\n204\t5. Tests drive the gate's new predicate, the trailer identity rule, the\n205\t   logged-session restriction, and the migration warn on a scaffold; the\n206\t   full suite stays green.\n207\t\n208\t### From WI-560 (Done-when 1 and 4, verbatim — 2 went to WI-580, 3 to WI-581; item 4 is shared)\n209\t\n210\t1. ONE shared definition of \"the last commit that could invalidate a\n211\t   verdict\" (excluding `docs/reviews`, `docs/log.d`, `docs/iteration`) is\n212\t   used by both the merge slot and the C2 review-owed derivation; the\n213\t   double-identical-round class becomes unrepresentable on a scaffold.\n214\t4. Tests drive all three.\n215\t\n216\t### From WI-559 (Done-when 2 and 3, verbatim — Done-when 1 went to WI-580; item 3 is shared with it)\n217\t\n218\t2. A committing ADJUDICATE session schedules its review round exactly as a\n219\t   committing BUILD does, and no exit banner claims a round that was never\n220\t   drawn.\n221\t3. Tests drive the false-partial class (built-and-verified lane, long\n222\t   suite) and the adjudicate round scheduling on a scaffold.\n223\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951f7d21-4e3c-4f81-ba38-e46e148acc62","uuid":"06599692-f539-477a-8e52-399fb4688cfb","timestamp":"2026-09-03T05:12:10.541Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-579-the-verdict-carrier-and-the-ad/docs/archive/work/complete/WI-579-the-verdict-carrier-and-the-ad.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-579\"\ntitle = \"The verdict carrier and the adjudication_review dial: gate over logged rounds, tree-bound trailer, generated rollup\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nspecref = \"\"\nbuildtier = \"strong\"\npriority = 9\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\nsupersedes = \"WI-558;WI-559;WI-560\"\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\nThe merge gate reads the EVIDENCE and the evidence names the tree it judged.\n\n`kitlib/verdict.py` (LLR-207, IF-175) is the verdict record's one home: the\nnon-record tree identity — a SHA-256 fold of `git ls-tree -r -z` with\n`docs/reviews/`, `docs/log.d/` and `docs/iteration/` dropped — the\n`Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>` trailer\ngrammar, the round-file / session-log join, and the branch-scoped readers. Two\ncallers stand on it and that is the point: `integrate._verdict_gate` (may this\nmerge?) and `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` (does this lane still owe a\nround?) asked one question with two rules over two exclusion sets, and the gap\nbetween them drew two identical rounds on WI-547.\n\n- **WI-558 DW1** — the gate computes over the branch's own round files,\n  restricted to rounds a LOGGED reviewer session produced: a file under\n  `docs/reviews/` is a round only when the coordinator's own committed session\n  log for that (train, ordinal) declares a REVIEW phase. Finding K closed —\n  an implementer cannot author its own approval without also forging the loop's\n  telemetry.\n- **WI-558 DW2** — the machine half rides the round's own record commit as a\n  trailer, written by the COORDINATOR and verified against its carrier's tree\n  (the `Bar-Gr
