{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011UoZ33L8zgec6DCEZLfV3F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: worker-lane-close-ritual-traps\n3\tdescription: \"Three traps a worker lane hits at C6 close — Deliverable must stay empty until the close commit, and two test reds that are trunk's or pre-existing, not yours\"\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 8876d3e3-9ead-4365-844a-04fd0bdeb9de\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\tMeasured on the WI-572 lane, 2026-09-01. All three recur for any worker lane.\n11\t\n12\t**1. Fill `## Deliverable` ONLY in the close commit.** `check_trajectory` errors\n13\t`R-A <WI>: status=active (open) but the Deliverable is non-empty (an open WI's\n14\tDeliverable is filled only at close)`, and the pre-commit hook REJECTS the\n15\tcommit. This collides with the standing-state rule (\"land the spec's\n16\tContext/Deliverable edits early\"): the Context half is safe, the Deliverable\n17\thalf is not. It reads the file ON DISK, so staging around it does not help —\n18\tpark the filled spec outside the repo and restore it at close.\n19\t**Why:** a filled Deliverable is the close signal; an open row carrying one is\n20\ta lie about its own state.\n21\t**How to apply:** land Context early; keep the Deliverable in the scratchpad\n22\tuntil the one commit that also clears `specref` and runs `spec_move.py`.\n23\t\n24\t**2. Amending a settled spine row reds `test_derive_stage.py::\n25\ttest_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`.** `docs/stage` is derived over\n26\tSETTLED rows, so amending an `Approved` row moves its fingerprint. Do NOT\n27\tregenerate: `docs/stage` is a declared generated artifact, every commit that\n28\tever wrote it is trunk-side bookkeeping, and the commit bar's own\n29\t`derived-stage --check` SKIPS on a work branch. Verify it is benign the cheap\n30\tway: `derive_stage.py --check` PRINTS the freshly derived `per-phase`,\n31\t`drafted` and `fingerprint` — if per-phase and drafted match what `docs/stage`\n32\talready records, only the input hash moved (confirmed again on WI-569,\n33\t2026-09-02, amending LLR-203/204). Note it is CAUSED-but-benign, not\n34\tinherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n35\t\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are\n36\t`kitlib/stage.py` `DECLARED_INPUTS`, so ANY cell edit moves the hash.\n37\tThe node is in `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`, so the smoke commit bar never sees it —\n38\tonly the full suite does.\n39\t\n40\t**3. Closing the LAST active claim reds `test_wi_convert.py::\n41\ttest_the_live_registry_round_trips_in_whichever_home_is_authoritative`** on\n42\t`docs/work/cancelled/README.md: does not start with a +++ frontmatter fence`.\n43\tWith a claim in flight the converter refuses by name (`drained-stop`) and the\n44\ttest passes on that branch; drained, it runs the real folder round-trip and\n45\tmeets a README the walker does not skip. Pre-existing — reproduces at trunk\n46\tcommits with no `docs/work/active/` at all.\n47\t\n48\t**How to apply (2 and 3):** report both reds with their provenance rather than\n49\tchasing them or claiming green. Bisect the single test in a `git worktree` at\n50\tthe prior commit — that is what separates \"inherited\" from \"caused\", and it is\n51\tcheap.\n52\t\n53\t**4. The close is itself an input change — re-verify gating claims at the FINAL\n54\ttip.** Draining `docs/work/active/` empties `integrate._claimed_specs`, so any\n55\trung reading the claimed specs answers differently after the close than at the\n56\tpre-close staged tree where a build session naturally checks it. On WI-572 that\n57\tdecided whether the branch got the `_adjudication_lane` exemption from its own\n58\tapproval-act refusal — checked pre-close it was one question, at the tip\n59\tanother. Same trap produced the stale headline harness figure: the recorded\n60\t\"full suite\" numbers were pre-close/pre-rework and no longer matched the tree an\n61\tintegrator merges.\n62\t**Why:** the tree the integrator sees is the only one a merge-gating claim is\n63\tworth anything at; a verification at an intermediate commit is a different\n64\ttree's answer.\n65\t**How to apply:** on a resumed session over an already-closed lane, re-run the\n66\tlane's own gating readers and the full suite at the tip before trusting the\n67\tfragment, and record the tip's numbers alongside (not over) the earlier reading.\n68\tRelated: [[supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons]],\n69\t[[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]],\n70\t[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951f7d21-4e3c-4f81-ba38-e46e148acc62","uuid":"899a39b7-ce27-4b11-ad73-196716eaafc8","timestamp":"2026-09-03T05:53:28.274Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md","content":"---\nname: worker-lane-close-ritual-traps\ndescription: \"Three traps a worker lane hits at C6 close — Deliverable must stay empty until the close commit, and two test reds that are trunk's or pre-existing, not yours\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 8876d3e3-9ead-4365-844a-04fd0bdeb9de\n---\n\nMeasured on the WI-572 lane, 2026-09-01. All three recur for any worker lane.\n\n**1. Fill `## Deliverable` ONLY in the close commit.** `check_trajectory` errors\n`R-A <WI>: status=active (open) but the Deliverable is non-empty (an open WI's\nDeliverable is filled only at close)`, and the pre-commit hook REJECTS the\ncommit. This collides with the standing-state rule (\"land the spec's\nContext/Deliverable edits early\"): the Context half is safe, the Deliverable\nhalf is not. It reads the file ON DISK, so staging around it does not help —\npark the filled spec outside the repo and restore it at close.\n**Why:** a filled Deliverable is the close signal; an open row carrying one is\na lie about its own state.\n**How to apply:** land Context early; keep the Deliverable in the scratchpad\nuntil the one commit that also clears `specref` and runs `spec_move.py`.\n\n**2. Amending a settled spine row reds `test_derive_stage.py::\ntest_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`.** `docs/stage` is derived over\nSETTLED rows, so amending an `Approved` row moves its fingerprint. Do NOT\nregenerate: `docs/stage` is a declared generated artifact, every commit that\never wrote it is trunk-side bookkeeping, and the commit bar's own\n`derived-stage --check` SKIPS on a work branch. Verify it is benign the cheap\nway: `derive_stage.py --check` PRINTS the freshly derived `per-phase`,\n`drafted` and `fingerprint` — if per-phase and drafted match what `docs/stage`\nalready records, only the input hash moved (confirmed again on WI-569,\n2026-09-02, amending LLR-203/204). Note it is CAUSED-but-benign, not\ninherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are\n`kitlib/stage.py` `DECLARED_INPUTS`, so ANY cell edit moves the hash.\nThe node is in `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`, so the smoke commit bar never sees it —\nonly the full suite does.\n\n**3. Closing the LAST active claim reds `test_wi_convert.py::\ntest_the_live_registry_round_trips_in_whichever_home_is_authoritative`** on\n`docs/work/cancelled/README.md: does not start with a +++ frontmatter fence`.\nWith a claim in flight the converter refuses by name (`drained-stop`) and the\ntest passes on that branch; drained, it runs the real folder round-trip and\nmeets a README the walker does not skip. Pre-existing — reproduces at trunk\ncommits with no `docs/work/active/` at all.\n\n**How to apply (2 and 3):** report both reds with their provenance rather than\nchasing them or claiming green. Bisect the single test in a `git worktree` at\nthe prior commit — that is what separates \"inherited\" from \"caused\", and it is\ncheap.\n\n**4. The close is itself an input change — re-verify gating claims at the FINAL\ntip.** Draining `docs/work/active/` empties `integrate._claimed_specs`, so any\nrung reading the claimed specs answers differently after the close than at the\npre-close staged tree where a build session naturally checks it. On WI-572 that\ndecided whether the branch got the `_adjudication_lane` exemption from its own\napproval-act refusal — checked pre-close it was one question, at the tip\nanother. Same trap produced the stale headline harness figure: the recorded\n\"full suite\" numbers were pre-close/pre-rework and no longer matched the tree an\nintegrator merges.\n**Why:** the tree the integrator sees is the only one a merge-gating claim is\nworth anything at; a verification at an intermediate commit is a different\ntree's answer.\n**How to apply:** on a resumed session over an already-closed lane, re-run the\nlane's own gating readers and the full suite at the tip before trusting the\nfragment, and record the tip's numbers alongside (not over) the earlier reading.\nRelated: [[supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons]],\n[[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
