{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefzBsvbMDLXzfp6yGhn8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LqUEXadECN2mkdLPUTfpSS","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md","old_string":"inherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are","new_string":"inherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". WATCH THE WORDING, not just the bisect — on WI-579 the phrase\n\"bisected clean at the integration base\" rode three review rounds unchallenged\nwhile meaning the OPPOSITE of how it read (the base is clean ⇒ the branch\nCAUSED it), functioning as an excuse. Write \"CAUSED by this branch, benign\nbecause <stated mechanism>\", never a sentence whose subject is ambiguous.\n`low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2208,"cache_read_input_tokens":213262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2208},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951f7d21-4e3c-4f81-ba38-e46e148acc62","uuid":"5814cf7b-a379-4115-9ebe-ac87b8225ce2","request_id":"req_011CefzBrmtCm1gecMDQ1qpR"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqUEXadECN2mkdLPUTfpSS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951f7d21-4e3c-4f81-ba38-e46e148acc62","uuid":"4deed529-957d-403b-bb71-b51d99f59291","timestamp":"2026-09-03T05:53:38.028Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md","oldString":"inherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are","newString":"inherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". WATCH THE WORDING, not just the bisect — on WI-579 the phrase\n\"bisected clean at the integration base\" rode three review rounds unchallenged\nwhile meaning the OPPOSITE of how it read (the base is clean ⇒ the branch\nCAUSED it), functioning as an excuse. Write \"CAUSED by this branch, benign\nbecause <stated mechanism>\", never a sentence whose subject is ambiguous.\n`low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are","originalFile":"---\nname: worker-lane-close-ritual-traps\ndescription: \"Three traps a worker lane hits at C6 close — Deliverable must stay empty until the close commit, and two test reds that are trunk's or pre-existing, not yours\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 8876d3e3-9ead-4365-844a-04fd0bdeb9de\n---\n\nMeasured on the WI-572 lane, 2026-09-01. All three recur for any worker lane.\n\n**1. Fill `## Deliverable` ONLY in the close commit.** `check_trajectory` errors\n`R-A <WI>: status=active (open) but the Deliverable is non-empty (an open WI's\nDeliverable is filled only at close)`, and the pre-commit hook REJECTS the\ncommit. This collides with the standing-state rule (\"land the spec's\nContext/Deliverable edits early\"): the Context half is safe, the Deliverable\nhalf is not. It reads the file ON DISK, so staging around it does not help —\npark the filled spec outside the repo and restore it at close.\n**Why:** a filled Deliverable is the close signal; an open row carrying one is\na lie about its own state.\n**How to apply:** land Context early; keep the Deliverable in the scratchpad\nuntil the one commit that also clears `specref` and runs `spec_move.py`.\n\n**2. Amending a settled spine row reds `test_derive_stage.py::\ntest_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`.** `docs/stage` is derived over\nSETTLED rows, so amending an `Approved` row moves its fingerprint. Do NOT\nregenerate: `docs/stage` is a declared generated artifact, every commit that\never wrote it is trunk-side bookkeeping, and the commit bar's own\n`derived-stage --check` SKIPS on a work branch. Verify it is benign the cheap\nway: `derive_stage.py --check` PRINTS the freshly derived `per-phase`,\n`drafted` and `fingerprint` — if per-phase and drafted match what `docs/stage`\nalready records, only the input hash moved (confirmed again on WI-569,\n2026-09-02, amending LLR-203/204). Note it is CAUSED-but-benign, not\ninherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as\n\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are\n`kitlib/stage.py` `DECLARED_INPUTS`, so ANY cell edit moves the hash.\nThe node is in `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`, so the smoke commit bar never sees it —\nonly the full suite does.\n\n**3. Closing the LAST active claim reds `test_wi_convert.py::\ntest_the_live_registry_round_trips_in_whichever_home_is_authoritative`** on\n`docs/work/cancelled/README.md: does not start with a +++ frontmatter fence`.\nWith a claim in flight the converter refuses by name (`drained-stop`) and the\ntest passes on that branch; drained, it runs the real folder round-trip and\nmeets a README the walker does not skip. Pre-existing — reproduces at trunk\ncommits with no `docs/work/active/` at all.\n\n**How to apply (2 and 3):** report both reds with their provenance rather than\nchasing them or claiming green. Bisect the single test in a `git worktree` at\nthe prior commit — that is what separates \"inherited\" from \"caused\", and it is\ncheap.\n\n**4. The close is itself an input change — re-verify gating claims at the FINAL\ntip.** Draining `docs/work/active/` empties `integrate._claimed_specs`, so any\nrung reading the claimed specs answers differently after the close than at the\npre-close staged tree where a build session naturally checks it. On WI-572 that\ndecided whether the branch got the `_adjudication_lane` exemption from its own\napproval-act refusal — checked pre-close it was one question, at the tip\nanother. Same trap produced the stale headline harness figure: the recorded\n\"full suite\" numbers were pre-close/pre-rework and no longer matched the tree an\nintegrator merges.\n**Why:** the tree the integrator sees is the only one a merge-gating claim is\nworth anything at; a verification at an intermediate commit is a different\ntree's answer.\n**How to apply:** on a resumed session over an already-closed lane, re-run the\nlane's own gating readers and the full suite at the tip before trusting the\nfragment, and record the tip's numbers alongside (not over) the earlier reading.\nRelated: [[supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons]],\n[[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]],\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":32,"oldLines":7,"newStart":32,"newLines":12,"lines":[" already records, only the input hash moved (confirmed again on WI-569,"," 2026-09-02, amending LLR-203/204). Note it is CAUSED-but-benign, not"," inherited: the node passes at the integration base, so do not report it as","-\"trunk's\". `low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are","+\"trunk's\". WATCH THE WORDING, not just the bisect — on WI-579 the phrase","+\"bisected clean at the integration base\" rode three review rounds unchallenged","+while meaning the OPPOSITE of how it read (the base is clean ⇒ the branch","+CAUSED it), functioning as an excuse. Write \"CAUSED by this branch, benign","+because <stated mechanism>\", never a sentence whose subject is ambiguous.","+`low-level-requirements.toml` and its five sibling registries are"," `kitlib/stage.py` `DECLARED_INPUTS`, so ANY cell edit moves the hash."," The node is in `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`, so the smoke commit bar never sees it —"," only the full suite does."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CefzCbAJtyNT8nptRN1v5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-579 rework is closed. Five commits, working tree clean, spec in `docs/archive/work/complete/`, final commit carries `WI: WI-579`.\n\n## What the round-015 findings turned out to be\n\nFour of the five were **one defect**: a definition stated once and then *recomputed* somewhere else with a piece left out. The composed rule is `governing_identity` = non-record fold + refresh peel; four separate readers were calling the bare fold instead.\n\n- **BLOCKER** — `round_entries` bound a round by `tree_identity(reviewed sha)` while the gate governs by `governing_identity`. A round drawn *after* a station refresh cites the post-refresh sha and is governed by the peeled pre-refresh tree, so the two were permanently unequal — the round invisible to both readers, an identical one re-drawn every tick. `governing_rev`/`governing_identity` now take the rev as an argument; the second rev-choice is **deleted**, not compensated for.\n- **MAJOR** — `commit_telemetry`'s empty-carrier arm swapped the pathspec for `--allow-empty`, and a pathspec-less `git commit` reads the whole index. Confirmed in a scratch repo that the two flags compose, so the path scope now survives both arms.\n- **MAJOR** — `gen_verdict_rollup --check` reported an extra rollup as stale that the write path never removed: an unclearable red on the pre-commit floor. The generator now owns its directory.\n- Two MINORs (uncovered TC-206 arm, the trailer's third rev-choice) closed alongside.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**I fixed a fifth site the review didn't name.** Sweeping every remaining `tree_identity` call turned up `integrate._legacy_rollup_refusal` making the identical rev-choice. I fixed it in-lane rather than filing it — shipping a known instance of the defect the round exists to close seemed worse than the scope stretch. It's called out explicitly in its own commit and the fragment, so it's easy to reject if you disagree.\n\n**I retracted a claim from earlier rounds.** The full suite's one failure is `test_derive_stage.py`, which rounds 007 and 012 recorded as *\"bisected clean at the integration base.\"* I drove the base in a scratch worktree: it **passes**. So that red is caused by this branch's spine edits, not inherited — the earlier phrasing read as an excuse while technically meaning the opposite. It's still benign (`docs/stage` is a trunk-owned generated artifact, `git diff base..HEAD -- docs/stage` is empty, and `check.py` skips the step on a work branch by design), but the Deliverable now says *caused-but-benign* with the mechanism stated.\n\n## Verification\n\nEvery new test was watched **red against the pre-fix code** before being kept, and red at the finding's own assertion — not merely red. Full unfiltered suite at `2b4be13c`: **3345 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 612.94s** (the `docs/stage` node above). Smoke at the closing tip: **1506 passed, 8 skipped in 32.72s**, budget **47.6s vs 60s**. No ratchet bump taken — `agent_common`'s +3 was compacted away, and `integrate` was re-stamped *downward* 1352→1351.\n\nNo `Status` was flipped and no `docs/archive/last_approved/` written; all touched spine rows stay `Drafted`, and the approval brief was regenerated at the amendments."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":215470,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"951f7d21-4e3c-4f81-ba38-e46e148acc62","uuid":"8f19065d-4073-4603-b5ae-dfa77a767dc2","request_id":"req_011CefzCa7Jurv9KByZvnAU1"}
